==English==

===Etymology===
From a phonetic spelling of {{m|en|love}} + {{m|en|-y}}; in the second sense, because this is perceived as a common utterance of thespians.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|luvvies}}

# {{lb|en|informal}} An affectionate term of address.
#: ''Don't cry '''luvvy''', everything will be OK''.
#{{lb|en|chiefly|British|humorous|sometimes|derogatory}} an [[actor]] or [[actress]], especially a [[narcissistic]] and [[pretentious]] one.


